---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { OPERATOR, TAKEDOWN_EMAIL } from '../data/site.js';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy · beforegta6.wtf"
  description="What beforegta6.wtf collects about visitors, and what it does not."
  path="/privacy/"
>
  <article class="prose">
    <h1 class="page-title">Privacy</h1>
    <p>
      beforegta6.wtf is a hobby site by {OPERATOR}, Belgium. Questions or requests:
      <a href={`mailto:${TAKEDOWN_EMAIL}`}>{TAKEDOWN_EMAIL}</a>.
    </p>
    <h2>What this site collects</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>There are no accounts and no forms. This site sets no cookies of its own.</li>
      <li>
        Page views are counted with Umami, which runs on our own server. Umami uses no cookies and
        does not store your IP address.
      </li>
      <li>
        Cloudflare delivers the site. It processes your IP address to do that and to block attacks (
        <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" rel="noopener">
          Cloudflare privacy policy
        </a>
        ).
      </li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Ads</h2>
    <p>
      There are no ads yet. Before Google AdSense goes live, this page will say what Google collects
      and how you can refuse it.
    </p>
    <h2>Links</h2>
    <p>
      Every card links to a post on another site, such as Reddit, X, YouTube or TikTok. Those sites
      have their own privacy policies.
    </p>
    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      Under the GDPR you can ask what we hold about you, and ask us to delete it. You can also
      complain to the Belgian Data Protection Authority (
      <a href="https://www.dataprotectionauthority.be" rel="noopener">
        dataprotectionauthority.be
      </a>
      ).
    </p>
    <p>
      <small>
        Last updated: <time datetime="2026-11-13">13 November 2026</time>.
      </small>
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
